%description:
Tests the ACE value 0b000 on the ACK of the SYN-ACK: the tester clears the
ACE field of A002. RFC 9768 Table 4 says that the path bleached the flags, so
the server "MUST NOT set ECT on outgoing packets and MUST NOT respond to
AccECN feedback" (section 3.2.2.1): B004 is Not-ECT, and the server does not
respond to the CE mark that A004 reports. As a data receiver, the server
still sends the ACE field (ACE 5 on B002).

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 1000"
*.*_tcp.accEcnOptionEnabled = false # the ACE field alone (tcp_accecn_option_* test the option)
*.*_tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"
*.srv_app.sendScript="2.0 1000; 3.0 1000"
*.tcptester.script="a2 ace 0; b3 ce"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[0.001 A001] A.1000 > B.2000: S E W N 0:0(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize
srv_tcp: LISTEN --> SYN_RCVD  (on RCV_SYN)
[0.003 B001] A.1000 < B.2000: A S W 500:500(0) ack 1 win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize
cli_tcp: SYN_SENT --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_SYN_ACK)
[0.005 A002] A.1000 > B.2000: A ack 501 win 16384 # changing ACE bits
srv_tcp: SYN_RCVD --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_ACK)
[1.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A E N 1:1001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 ECT(0) 
[1.203 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A E N ack 1001 win 16384 
[2.001 B003] A.1000 < B.2000: A E N 501:1501(1000) ack 1001 win 16384 CE # marking CE
[2.203 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A W N ack 1501 win 16384 
[3.001 B004] A.1000 < B.2000: A E N 1501:2501(1000) ack 1001 win 16384 
[3.203 A005] A.1000 > B.2000: A W N ack 2501 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
AccECN: the ACK of the SYN-ACK has ACE 0, no ECT and no response to the feedback
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
AccECN: ACE=6, packets acknowledged=1, new CE marks=1 (mod 8: 1)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
AccECN: no response to the feedback, because the ACK of the SYN-ACK had ACE 0
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
